---
import Frame from '../components/PageFrame.astro';
const items = [
  {
    title: 'Accessible from the start',
    body: 'Visible focus, native controls and readable status messages make actions understandable beyond a screenshot.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Responsive by intent',
    body: 'Content order and flexible layouts give a phone the same meaningful journey as a larger screen.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Motion with a purpose',
    body: 'Brief state transitions support understanding. Reduced-motion preferences keep the experience calm.',
  },
];
---

<Frame label="Experience" items={items}>
  <section class="container section split-section" id="principles">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">DETAILS THAT DO A JOB</p>
      <h2>Make the next action feel obvious.</h2>
      <p>
        A clear label tells you what will happen. A visible focus ring shows
        where you are. A status message explains what changed. These details are
        part of the interface’s meaning.
      </p>
      <p>
        Try the native controls here with Tab, Space and Enter. The examples
        work without a custom component framework; their labels stay associated
        with the controls.
      </p>
      <p class="demo-note">
        Accessibility is an ongoing practice. Automated checks and keyboard
        testing do not replace testing with people and assistive technology.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="principle-gallery">
      <h3>A few useful interaction details</h3>
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" checked />
        <span>Show context before a decision</span>
      </label>
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" />
        <span>Keep the original source nearby</span>
      </label>
      <details>
        <summary>What makes a state change clear?</summary>
        <p>
          Text explains the new state, the relevant control remains available,
          and meaning is not carried by colour alone. Open a product demo to see
          this applied.
        </p>
      </details>
      <a class="text-link" href="/products/workflows/#demo">
        Try the approval interaction →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section split-section">
    <div class="reading">
      <p class="eyebrow">CONTENT BEFORE DECORATION</p>
      <h2>Responsive means reconsidered.</h2>
      <p>
        On a narrow screen, the proposition comes before the sample interface.
        Cards stack into a readable sequence. Dense comparison tables scroll
        within their own labelled region, while surrounding content reflows.
      </p>
      <p>
        Long headings can wrap rather than disappear beyond the viewport. Touch
        targets have space around them. Navigation can scroll in a short
        landscape window.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="reading">
      <p class="eyebrow">MORE THAN COLOUR</p>
      <h2>Let the information do the work.</h2>
      <p>
        Workflow stages include written statuses. Knowledge results identify
        sources. Insights offers a chart description and the exact values in a
        table. A person can check the same information through more than one
        representation.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site honours reduced-motion preferences and keeps reading
        independent of entrance animations.
      </p>
      <a
        class="text-link"
        href="/journal/website-redesign-checklist-for-malaysian-smes/"
      >
        Use the SME website checklist →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Frame>
